1
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:07,400
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

2
00:00:09,533 --> 00:00:11,500
Huh...

3
00:00:11,500 --> 00:00:13,000
No...

4
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:16,233
No, I really am going to have to
go back and kill them, aren't I?

5
00:00:16,233 --> 00:00:19,200
Y'know, I don't want to
have to do this, but...

6
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,667
Okay, let's be fair. If I'm going
to be judge, jury, and executioner,

7
00:00:22,667 --> 00:00:24,367
I can at least listen to the jury.

8
00:00:24,367 --> 00:00:25,933
Let's do one more lap.

9
00:00:25,933 --> 00:00:28,967
Is there ANY conceivable way out of here?

10
00:00:28,967 --> 00:00:30,867
I'm not even seeing a ladder.

11
00:00:30,867 --> 00:00:33,600
I could climb up out of
here and leave the boat,

12
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,433
but they didn't say anything about that.

13
00:00:35,433 --> 00:00:38,333
He was talking like it's right
around the corner--it's not!

14
00:00:38,333 --> 00:00:41,367
Okay, I'll be generous. I am SO generous.

15
00:00:41,367 --> 00:00:43,733
Okay, that's one lap--I'm
going to go kill them.

16
00:00:43,733 --> 00:00:45,500
But let's assume they DIDN'T know

17
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:48,800
this was a kill box with multiple
rocket launchers ready for me.

18
00:00:48,800 --> 00:00:50,533
Then why else would they send me here?

19
00:00:50,533 --> 00:00:53,967
Just to watch me do laps in a dead
end, and have a laugh about it?

20
00:00:53,967 --> 00:00:56,100
No. They're dead. I'm going to go kill them.

21
00:00:56,100 --> 00:01:00,300
I have no leads, no information...
and, apparently, no allies.

22
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,767
So let's stop pretending.

23
00:01:01,767 --> 00:01:02,392
Gun it!

24
00:01:05,233 --> 00:01:07,633
Yeah, there we go. There we go.

25
00:01:07,633 --> 00:01:08,600
Oh, this thing...

26
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:10,300
Yeah.

27
00:01:10,833 --> 00:01:13,400
That's not happening again. Ever.

28
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:16,067
I still wish I had how much ammo this has.

29
00:01:16,067 --> 00:01:16,833
[distant gunfire]
Dammit.

30
00:01:16,833 --> 00:01:17,833
[distant gunfire]
They're still there...

31
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:21,000
All right, y'know what? This can wait.

32
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:24,667
It doesn't REALLY matter if I
kill them today or do it tomorrow.

33
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:28,367
This might be one of those
work-smarter-not-harder situations.

34
00:01:28,367 --> 00:01:31,900
Although th--oof--this kind
of illustrates the point.

35
00:01:31,900 --> 00:01:35,600
I didn't kill THOSE cops and here
they are still giving me trouble.

36
00:01:35,600 --> 00:01:37,833
I need to be able to
kill people with my mind.

37
00:01:37,833 --> 00:01:41,200
Black Mesa was working on that,
but they didn't get very far.

38
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:45,500
The equipment was really bulky;
it used a ridiculous amount of power;

39
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,800
and even then, the most they were
able to do was kill a small dog.

40
00:01:48,800 --> 00:01:50,567
It just wasn't panning out.

41
00:01:50,567 --> 00:01:54,133
Y'know, if we had better battery power
that would open up a lot of doors.

42
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:57,433
So am I spending the night up there, or...?

43
00:01:57,433 --> 00:01:59,700
Oh wait, is that a passageway?

44
00:01:59,700 --> 00:02:01,800
Well, I'm not getting the boat up there.

45
00:02:02,467 --> 00:02:04,146
Or am I?!

46
00:02:04,733 --> 00:02:06,067
OR AM I--?!

47
00:02:07,300 --> 00:02:10,167
Time to solve this the way
I seem to solve everything.

48
00:02:12,267 --> 00:02:13,833
Oh-ho!

49
00:02:13,833 --> 00:02:14,967
Oh!

50
00:02:15,567 --> 00:02:16,367
Yep.

51
00:02:16,367 --> 00:02:17,233
YEP!

52
00:02:17,233 --> 00:02:18,167
No...!

53
00:02:18,167 --> 00:02:19,100
NO!

54
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:21,800
Okay, that's okay. I can work with this.

55
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:25,133
Even though I'm still using
the wrong tool for the job.

56
00:02:25,133 --> 00:02:29,333
They never should have given me a boat.
This is just a joke that won't end.

57
00:02:29,333 --> 00:02:30,700
I mean--OOF!

58
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:32,333
OH!

59
00:02:32,333 --> 00:02:34,267
OH-HO-HO!

60
00:02:34,267 --> 00:02:36,167
Look at how amazing I am!

61
00:02:36,167 --> 00:02:40,700
I out-engineered a problem that wouldn't
exist if I wasn't in a fucking boat!

62
00:02:40,700 --> 00:02:41,767
Oof!

63
00:02:41,767 --> 00:02:42,833
UFF!

64
00:02:42,833 --> 00:02:44,267
I mean, seriously.

65
00:02:44,267 --> 00:02:46,600
Yeah, it's closed. Of course it is.

66
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:48,733
Has there been one situation today

67
00:02:48,733 --> 00:02:51,433
where I wouldn't have been
better served by a quad bike?

68
00:02:51,433 --> 00:02:54,167
That's probably why I got
the boat: Nobody wants it.

69
00:02:54,167 --> 00:02:56,900
I'm like a kid that can't
accept that winter's over,

70
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:59,000
so I'm taking a sled down a muddy embankment

71
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,733
that has a tiny patch of snow left.

72
00:03:01,733 --> 00:03:02,867
Oof.

73
00:03:02,867 --> 00:03:05,167
There's no--AUGH!

74
00:03:05,167 --> 00:03:06,767
That one hurt...

75
00:03:06,767 --> 00:03:08,167
Fuck...

76
00:03:08,167 --> 00:03:10,867
But that's been my boating experience.

77
00:03:10,867 --> 00:03:13,433
Just a fish flopping around in a puddle.

78
00:03:13,433 --> 00:03:15,167
With people shooting at me.

79
00:03:15,167 --> 00:03:16,533
And missing a lot.

80
00:03:16,533 --> 00:03:18,367
Because I'm a floppy fish.

81
00:03:18,367 --> 00:03:20,067
Y'know, I've lowered my expectations

82
00:03:20,067 --> 00:03:23,767
of how the world is going to recognize
my genius since I've come back.

83
00:03:23,767 --> 00:03:29,867
So if, on my tombstone, all it says is
'He was a dead, floppy fish', I'll understand.

84
00:03:29,867 --> 00:03:32,567
Eh, I'm fooling myself.
They won't bury me.

85
00:03:32,567 --> 00:03:33,700
[alarms sound]
They'll just--

86
00:03:33,700 --> 00:03:35,967
Why are--oof! Why are there sirens?

87
00:03:35,967 --> 00:03:37,933
OH! MAN THE CANNONS!

88
00:03:37,933 --> 00:03:39,667
C'mon, c'mon, C'MON!

89
00:03:39,667 --> 00:03:41,500
How am I missing him?!

90
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,400
OH! YOU'RE ON FIRE!

91
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:45,567
FUCK YOU! YOU'RE ON FIRE!

92
00:03:45,567 --> 00:03:47,167
No, I'M on fire.

93
00:03:47,167 --> 00:03:48,733
GOING DOWN!

94
00:03:48,733 --> 00:03:51,100
YOU'RE GOIN' DOWN!

95
00:03:51,100 --> 00:03:52,800
LET'S GO MOP HIM UP!

96
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:54,333
OH, HE'S STILL UP!

97
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:55,167
I'LL HELP!

98
00:03:55,167 --> 00:03:56,300
I'M HELPING!

99
00:03:56,300 --> 00:03:57,200
JAMMED!

100
00:03:57,200 --> 00:03:59,900
GAAAH! OH NO NO NO NO NO!

101
00:03:59,900 --> 00:04:02,333
NO NO! I ALMOST HAVE HIM!

102
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:05,633
OH MY GOD! RAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAH!

103
00:04:06,333 --> 00:04:10,567
OH! I'M GONNA EAT YOU! I'M GONNA
EAT YOUR WHOLE FUCKING CHOPPER!

104
00:04:10,567 --> 00:04:12,933
I DON'T CARE IF IT'S BAD FOR MY TEETH!

105
00:04:12,933 --> 00:04:15,000
BUT I'M GONNA GET BEHIND THIS ROCK FIRST,

106
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:17,100
[alarms sound]
because being shot is the worst w--

107
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:18,533
[alarms sound]

108
00:04:18,533 --> 00:04:19,158
What's he doing?

109
00:04:19,158 --> 00:04:21,000
[multiple explosions]

110
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:21,733
[multiple explosions]
How many of...

111
00:04:21,733 --> 00:04:24,200
[multiple explosions]

112
00:04:24,200 --> 00:04:25,767
[multiple explosions]
No, no...! Come on!

113
00:04:25,767 --> 00:04:28,167
[multiple explosions]
I'm a physicist! This isn't possible!

114
00:04:28,167 --> 00:04:30,937
[multiple explosions]
This is just basic mass conservation!

115
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:33,986
[machine gun fire]
GAAAAH! NO! STOP! FIRING!

116
00:04:33,986 --> 00:04:35,767
RRRRAAAAAAAAAAGH!

117
00:04:35,767 --> 00:04:36,933
THIS ISN'T FAIR!

118
00:04:36,933 --> 00:04:39,233
YOU SHOT AT ME FIFTY TIMES BEFORE THIS!

119
00:04:39,233 --> 00:04:42,800
SO I SHOULD GET TO SHOOT YOU FIFTY
TIMES BEFORE YOU GET TO SHOOT BACK!

120
00:04:42,800 --> 00:04:46,000
I REALIZE YOU DON'T HAVE ANY
MORE MINES, BUT JUST STOP SHOOT--

121
00:04:47,033 --> 00:04:49,185
[multiple explosions]
Wait, you DO have more mines?

122
00:04:49,185 --> 00:04:49,467
[multiple explosions]
What...?

123
00:04:49,467 --> 00:04:50,600
[multiple explosions]

124
00:04:50,600 --> 00:04:52,600
[multiple explosions]
This is like a magic trick.

125
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,933
[multiple explosions]
This guy wanted to be a magician

126
00:04:53,933 --> 00:04:55,967
[multiple explosions]
but he became a fighter pilot.

127
00:04:55,967 --> 00:04:57,400
[multiple explosions]
It's a good act.

128
00:04:57,400 --> 00:04:59,533
[multiple explosions]
I'm going to be thinking about this.

129
00:04:59,533 --> 00:05:02,567
[multiple explosions]
A LITTLE LOUD, THOUGH!

130
00:05:02,567 --> 00:05:04,767
[machine gun fire]
Oh, not the gun! Not that!

131
00:05:04,767 --> 00:05:06,233
[machine gun fire]
Nobody wants that!

132
00:05:06,233 --> 00:05:07,000
[machine gun fire]
See, this is why

133
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,900
[machine gun fire]
you couldn't hack it on stage,

134
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:10,667
[machine gun fire]
because of shit like this.

135
00:05:10,667 --> 00:05:12,506
Yeah, try to escape THIS, Houdini.

136
00:05:13,733 --> 00:05:15,100
HE'S STILL ON FIRE!

137
00:05:16,167 --> 00:05:18,867
We make good choppers in the future!

138
00:05:18,867 --> 00:05:21,167
YEAH, GET IN CLOSE! LET'S DO THIS!

139
00:05:21,167 --> 00:05:24,433
WHOA! YOU ALMOST DROPPED THAT IN MY LAP!

140
00:05:24,433 --> 00:05:27,600
THAT'S PRETTY GOOD! YOU
KNOW HOW TO PUT ON A SHOW!

141
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:29,467
Just fucking die already.

142
00:05:29,467 --> 00:05:30,900
OH!

143
00:05:30,900 --> 00:05:32,400
OHHHHH!

144
00:05:32,400 --> 00:05:33,933
ENCORE!

145
00:05:33,933 --> 00:05:36,033
ENCORE, YOU FUCK!

146
00:05:37,267 --> 00:05:40,700
Oh! This was SO not worth it.

147
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:45,567
Well, it's that time again.
Confirmation kill time.

148
00:05:45,567 --> 00:05:52,867
My God, you've given me more trouble...
I think, than anyone! That's amazing!

149
00:05:52,867 --> 00:05:55,400
Okay, if he comes out wearing a top hat...

150
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:57,867
Well, I'm still going to kill
him. There's no other option.

151
00:05:57,867 --> 00:06:00,400
But I'll give him some
last words. I can do that.

152
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:04,100
And now, for my next trick:
Blam! Then I shoot him?

153
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,867
That would be a nice end to the day.

154
00:06:05,867 --> 00:06:08,500
Okay, seriously. I'm not
seeing any entry point.

155
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:10,733
It looks too small to hold someone.

156
00:06:10,733 --> 00:06:13,767
I mean, there's a body over there,
but wasn't that from earlier?

157
00:06:13,767 --> 00:06:16,500
I thought I saw something,
but I was distracted.

158
00:06:16,500 --> 00:06:19,833
Oh... This isn't what I want to see...

159
00:06:19,833 --> 00:06:22,933
I think this means it's controlled remotely.

160
00:06:22,933 --> 00:06:25,100
But then why did the body fall out?

161
00:06:25,100 --> 00:06:29,000
It kept flying and shooting after
that, so it wasn't even needed.

162
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,800
Is this a union thing? Like union law says

163
00:06:31,800 --> 00:06:35,533
there must be one employee present
in all remote-controlled helicopters?

164
00:06:35,533 --> 00:06:39,133
We're conquered by aliens, but
the police still have unions?

165
00:06:39,133 --> 00:06:41,500
Well, that's fucking humanity for you.

166
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:43,300
Is this another dead end?

167
00:06:43,300 --> 00:06:45,267
This is getting SO old.

168
00:06:45,267 --> 00:06:48,133
I really am going to have to
go back and kill them later.

169
00:06:48,133 --> 00:06:51,400
They sent me on a giant snipe
hunt. That's all this is.

170
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:54,633
If I get out of here, all that's going to
happen is I'll meet another one saying,

171
00:06:54,633 --> 00:06:58,700
"Oh, you're almost there. Just keep
going." I'll be at this for days.

172
00:06:59,967 --> 00:07:01,067
Well...

173
00:07:01,067 --> 00:07:02,533
[straining]
This seems to be--

174
00:07:02,533 --> 00:07:03,033
Whuh!

175
00:07:03,600 --> 00:07:06,167
[straining]
...seems to go somewhere.

176
00:07:07,233 --> 00:07:09,167
Ah! Splinter...

177
00:07:09,167 --> 00:07:11,567
[straining]
Why...do I have...to do...

178
00:07:11,567 --> 00:07:15,767
[straining]
...absolutely fucking everything?

179
00:07:15,767 --> 00:07:18,600
[exhaling]

180
00:07:18,600 --> 00:07:22,033
Y'know, if I go back, should I
just shoot them all immediately?

181
00:07:22,033 --> 00:07:23,667
That seems kind of wasteful.

182
00:07:23,667 --> 00:07:26,333
I bet if I shot one of them,
they would start talking.

183
00:07:26,333 --> 00:07:28,967
I could even do that thing
where I look at one person,

184
00:07:28,967 --> 00:07:31,400
then shoot someone else
with my peripheral vision,

185
00:07:31,400 --> 00:07:34,333
but I don't even turn my head;
I just keep staring at them.

186
00:07:34,333 --> 00:07:36,633
They seem soft. I think they'd break.

187
00:07:36,633 --> 00:07:39,733
But the real question is what
was going on with those mines?

188
00:07:39,733 --> 00:07:41,833
I mean, let's start with the obvious:

189
00:07:41,833 --> 00:07:46,933
It was impossible to fit that many
mines that size inside the chopper.

190
00:07:46,933 --> 00:07:48,833
But they came out of it!

191
00:07:48,833 --> 00:07:52,567
So I'm only seeing two
possibilities for what happened,

192
00:07:52,567 --> 00:07:56,200
and they're both a little
too crazy for my liking.

193
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:58,467
I don't like it when people out-crazy me.

194
00:07:58,467 --> 00:08:00,467
Dammit, is this another dead end?

195
00:08:00,467 --> 00:08:03,008
I am the king of dead ends today.

196
00:08:03,008 --> 00:08:05,600
Well, I am taking a boat on an empty river.

197
00:08:05,600 --> 00:08:08,333
It's like that saying: Up
shit creek without a paddle.

198
00:08:08,333 --> 00:08:10,567
I'm up shit creek without a creek.

199
00:08:10,567 --> 00:08:14,500
Oop! That ramp looks almost doable.

200
00:08:14,500 --> 00:08:16,333
Why not? Why not?

201
00:08:16,333 --> 00:08:21,267
I'm out of water, the boat
still exists, and so does land.

202
00:08:21,267 --> 00:08:22,833
My logic is impeccable.

203
00:08:22,833 --> 00:08:25,633
And once again, there's
no one here to film this.

204
00:08:25,633 --> 00:08:28,433
The world doesn't know what
it's losing from this invasion.

205
00:08:28,433 --> 00:08:29,450
Oooh...?!

206
00:08:30,167 --> 00:08:34,033
Okay! This officially makes me an amphibian.

207
00:08:34,033 --> 00:08:35,767
I mean, amphibious.

208
00:08:35,767 --> 00:08:37,467
The ground's not too rough.

209
00:08:37,467 --> 00:08:38,768
I should've done this earlier.

210
00:08:39,767 --> 00:08:42,467
Yeah, see, this is more my speed.

211
00:08:42,467 --> 00:08:42,967
Hup!

212
00:08:45,333 --> 00:08:49,067
Yeah, if I'm going to have enemies,
I like them running around confused,

213
00:08:49,067 --> 00:08:51,167
me not having to aim so much.

214
00:08:51,167 --> 00:08:53,000
I still could use a beer holder,

215
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:54,830
and more importantly, a beer.

216
00:08:54,830 --> 00:08:56,700
But I feel like we're making progress.

217
00:08:56,700 --> 00:08:59,600
Yeah, I can make my own beer
holder if that's the problem.

218
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,367
I just need to find some wire.

219
00:09:01,367 --> 00:09:03,967
Oh no way! It's the spook!

220
00:09:03,967 --> 00:09:06,041
Is he waving? Did he wave at me?

221
00:09:06,833 --> 00:09:09,867
Okay, well--WHOA! Well, he's right there.

222
00:09:09,867 --> 00:09:12,867
Is he really going to pull this
cat-and-mouse bullshit on me again?

223
00:09:12,867 --> 00:09:17,600
I kind of feel like he might, but it's
not like I have other places to be.

224
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:21,367
Yeah, scraping the pavement with the
boat--this is the definition of subtle.

225
00:09:21,367 --> 00:09:23,400
I might be making sparks.

226
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:26,500
Oh my God. He did it again, didn't he?

227
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:27,900
Yep. Nothing here.

228
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,400
What an asshole.

229
00:09:29,400 --> 00:09:31,500
What an asshole!

230
00:09:31,500 --> 00:09:35,133
It's even enough for him to watch;
he has to make sure I see him.

231
00:09:35,133 --> 00:09:38,667
I mean, what, did he do some urban
climbing in his suit and briefcase?

232
00:09:38,667 --> 00:09:41,267
I don't think so! He just
teleported out again!

233
00:09:41,267 --> 00:09:45,033
Y'know, wherever I end up sleeping, the
first thing I'm going to see when I wake up

234
00:09:45,033 --> 00:09:48,833
is his face outside a window
staring at me. I'd bet anything.

235
00:09:48,833 --> 00:09:53,300
You know what disturbs me the most is
I had a clean shot. I could've gone for it.

236
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:56,500
I wasn't even thinking about
that earlier, now I am.

237
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:59,933
But he KNEW that. He must
have, and he didn't care.

238
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:03,433
This guy's not an idiot. He's ready
for me to turn the guns on him.

239
00:10:03,433 --> 00:10:06,533
But I don't know how, which
is really pissing me off.

240
00:10:06,533 --> 00:10:10,267
But I know that he knows, and he knows
that I know, and the more we get together,

241
00:10:10,267 --> 00:10:12,033
the more I want to kill him.

242
00:10:12,033 --> 00:10:15,300
Yep, this is end of the line.
This whole thing was a setup.

243
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,300
They never expected me to get this far.

244
00:10:17,300 --> 00:10:18,900
Well, except for the spook.

245
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:19,833
What's this do?

246
00:10:20,867 --> 00:10:22,800
[alarms sound]
Uh oh.

247
00:10:22,800 --> 00:10:24,010
[alarms sound]
What?

248
00:10:24,010 --> 00:10:26,500
Oh. That's not as bad as I was expecting.

249
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,867
Does that help?

250
00:10:27,867 --> 00:10:30,500
No, it doesn't. The water's too low.

251
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:33,100
I mean there's no way I
would jump off a fucking dam,

252
00:10:33,100 --> 00:10:36,167
but I guess I could've sent the
boat over and hope it'd survive.

253
00:10:36,167 --> 00:10:38,600
Yeah, my damn memories aren't very good.

254
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:41,267
Last damn time was pretty awful, too.

255
00:10:41,267 --> 00:10:44,867
Damn, now everyone's going to think
I'm an asshole if I talk about this,

256
00:10:44,867 --> 00:10:46,033
because this is literally

257
00:10:46,033 --> 00:10:50,167
the SECOND time I've been attacked
by a helicopter over a dam.

258
00:10:50,167 --> 00:10:51,633
No one's going to believe that.

259
00:10:51,633 --> 00:10:55,133
They'll think I'm making this damn
thing up to sound cool. Dammit.

260
00:10:55,133 --> 00:10:58,033
Well, I'm abandoning the boat, again.

261
00:10:58,033 --> 00:11:00,633
Though the issue is I'm abandoning that gun.

262
00:11:00,633 --> 00:11:01,500
That gun...

263
00:11:01,933 --> 00:11:03,967
How much ammo did it have?

264
00:11:03,967 --> 00:11:06,767
Okay, okay, the real question is the mines,

265
00:11:06,767 --> 00:11:07,505
because...

266
00:11:08,400 --> 00:11:09,867
No, I don't want to eat that.

267
00:11:09,867 --> 00:11:12,100
What's in here? Something?

268
00:11:12,100 --> 00:11:13,967
Yes! Of course! Empty!

269
00:11:13,967 --> 00:11:14,933
Ngah!

270
00:11:14,933 --> 00:11:18,200
Why would they put the empty
bottles back in the refrigerator?!

271
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:21,667
That's just--UGH! AGH! OH MY GOD!

272
00:11:21,667 --> 00:11:24,033
THAT'S WORSE THAN THAT BODY FROM EARLIER!

273
00:11:24,033 --> 00:11:26,933
DON'T GO IN THE KITCHEN! JESUS!

274
00:11:27,933 --> 00:11:29,767
What was I thinking about?

275
00:11:29,767 --> 00:11:31,533
Of course! The mines!

276
00:11:31,533 --> 00:11:36,867
So option 1 is, the mines are just paper
thin shells that they keep folded up,

277
00:11:36,867 --> 00:11:40,667
then they're filled with some
explosive gas just before deploying.

278
00:11:40,667 --> 00:11:43,567
So it's like bunch of balloons
and a canister of helium.

279
00:11:43,567 --> 00:11:47,200
It's a party clown military. That's crazy.

280
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:50,233
And if they're going to do that, why not
just blast music while they're at it,

281
00:11:50,233 --> 00:11:51,800
like in "Apocalypse Now"?

282
00:11:51,800 --> 00:11:55,900
Eh, maybe they were worried the targets
would dance too much and be harder to hit.

283
00:11:55,900 --> 00:11:57,381
But option 2...

284
00:11:58,467 --> 00:12:02,767
The only other possibility I'm seeing
is they have teleporters so refined,

285
00:12:02,767 --> 00:12:07,267
they just teleport in the mines on demand
through some mechanism in the chopper.

286
00:12:07,267 --> 00:12:10,167
And that raises so many more questions.

287
00:12:10,167 --> 00:12:12,767
Oh. I must have dropped this.

288
00:12:12,767 --> 00:12:14,567
This is obviously mine.

289
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:19,300
So if they're actually teleporting in the
mines, that would explain some things.

290
00:12:19,300 --> 00:12:20,900
Like that gun they handed me.

291
00:12:20,900 --> 00:12:23,967
I honestly thought I would've
run out of ammo by now.

292
00:12:23,967 --> 00:12:26,442
The thing is, maybe I did!

293
00:12:27,300 --> 00:12:28,700
Again and again.

294
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:31,567
Maybe it wasn't overheating
but was out of ammo,

295
00:12:31,567 --> 00:12:35,867
so I had to wait on somebody in a warehouse
somewhere to load more into the teleporter.

296
00:12:35,867 --> 00:12:37,933
Like that armory scene in "The Matrix",

297
00:12:37,933 --> 00:12:41,400
except it's full of guys loading
munitions into teleporters all day.

298
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:43,967
Santa's OTHER workshop.

299
00:12:43,967 --> 00:12:46,633
Now I have to assume they
need some sort of receiver,

300
00:12:46,633 --> 00:12:50,167
because otherwise, why not just
teleport a bullet into my head?

301
00:12:50,167 --> 00:12:54,267
But if they can do that, that has
so much potential not being used.

302
00:12:54,267 --> 00:12:55,157
This way?

303
00:12:55,157 --> 00:12:56,333
[distant echoing voice]

304
00:12:56,333 --> 00:12:58,967
Shit, the sewer's talking again.

305
00:12:58,967 --> 00:13:00,300
Should I listen?

306
00:13:00,300 --> 00:13:03,400
DISTANT VOICE: You leap, you
fall, we see you flash between...

307
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:04,433
Hello?!

308
00:13:04,433 --> 00:13:05,333
Is it this one?

309
00:13:06,233 --> 00:13:06,826
No...

310
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:09,800
VOICE: Communion of the vortessence.

311
00:13:09,800 --> 00:13:12,167
VOICE: And that other: a deeper mystery.

312
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:12,833
What?

313
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:15,572
VOICE: No deeper than the void itself.

314
00:13:16,600 --> 00:13:17,333
No--

315
00:13:17,333 --> 00:13:23,000
VOICE: We have endured these chafing
bonds for eons, yet a single moment...

316
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:27,967
No... I found it's best to decline
invitations from sewer people.

317
00:13:27,967 --> 00:13:29,700
We don't float up here.

318
00:13:29,700 --> 00:13:32,967
I WOULD like to find shelter
before it gets dark, though,

319
00:13:32,967 --> 00:13:36,767
some place that's not going to get
stormed by backup troopers in 20 minutes.

320
00:13:36,767 --> 00:13:40,100
Okay, someone's been here.
What is this? Is this a test?

321
00:13:42,767 --> 00:13:45,967
Oh no... This has got to
be the rebel base, right?

322
00:13:45,967 --> 00:13:50,000
This is what they were sending me towards?
Some shanty town, but with lights?

323
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:53,133
It looks deserted; they must've
been raided before I got here.

324
00:13:53,133 --> 00:13:56,433
I'm not surprised. They're probably
being interrogated right now.

325
00:13:56,433 --> 00:13:58,533
Oh hell. One of those.

326
00:13:58,533 --> 00:14:01,400
Well, I'm definitely not
sleeping here tonight!

327
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:05,000
Yeah, I'm not seeing any bodies. They
must've just come in and grabbed them.

328
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:07,400
But, okay, if they can teleport in ammo,

329
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:10,367
why didn't they just drop
one serious bomb on me,

330
00:14:10,367 --> 00:14:12,267
something I couldn't run away from,

331
00:14:12,267 --> 00:14:14,933
rather than 200 large cherry bombs?

332
00:14:14,933 --> 00:14:18,500
Y'know, they're more advanced than
us, but I'm not sure they're smarter.

333
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:20,967
Because that helicopter armor was unreal,

334
00:14:20,967 --> 00:14:23,900
but as soon as I had one of their
guns, it was an even fight again.

335
00:14:23,900 --> 00:14:26,533
It's an arms race just to stay in place.

336
00:14:26,533 --> 00:14:27,733
Like Magic: The Gathering.

337
00:14:28,233 --> 00:14:29,100
Hm.

338
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:30,767
Well, here we are!

339
00:14:30,767 --> 00:14:33,867
If you go back in time and conquer
cavemen with a fighter jet,

340
00:14:33,867 --> 00:14:37,733
it doesn't matter how smart the cavemen
are, you still have a fighter jet.

341
00:14:37,733 --> 00:14:39,967
Okay, not this way.

342
00:14:39,967 --> 00:14:41,633
Yeah, I can do this.

343
00:14:41,633 --> 00:14:44,667
Hup-hup-HUP! There we go.

344
00:14:44,667 --> 00:14:48,600
Well, the aliens sure killed off a lot
of people who knew what they're doing.

345
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:50,017
I can tell that much.

346
00:14:50,017 --> 00:14:53,133
Oh shit. So maybe they're
smarter than I realized.

347
00:14:53,133 --> 00:14:55,600
Because maybe they killed
off everyone competent,

348
00:14:55,600 --> 00:14:59,433
then the people who were left came
up with the inflatable mines idea.

349
00:14:59,433 --> 00:15:01,267
Ehhhhh...

350
00:15:01,267 --> 00:15:04,467
Y'know, it sure is peaceful
since I left the boat.

351
00:15:04,467 --> 00:15:06,333
They put a tracker on it for sure.

352
00:15:06,333 --> 00:15:10,433
This would almost be nice if I hadn't
seen Cleveland levels of water pollution.

353
00:15:10,433 --> 00:15:14,067
My face HAS been feeling a
little itchy since I fell in.

354
00:15:14,067 --> 00:15:16,140
Oh, more wavelength graffiti, huh?

355
00:15:16,900 --> 00:15:20,733
I really am going to need a food
and water plan at some point, huh?

356
00:15:20,733 --> 00:15:23,822
I sort of forgot about
that. I've been distracted.

357
00:15:24,433 --> 00:15:25,300
No.

358
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:27,133
Y'know, I'm thinking back to high school,

359
00:15:27,133 --> 00:15:31,300
where the counselor asked you to think
about your future and what your plans are.

360
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:33,667
If I knew then what I know now,

361
00:15:33,667 --> 00:15:38,700
I would've just held up two middle fingers
and kept them there. Hang 'em high.

362
00:15:38,700 --> 00:15:41,567
I should've listened to Eddie
about joining that militia.

363
00:15:41,567 --> 00:15:45,667
I mean, he wasn't wrong, he was
just way too soon was the problem.

364
00:15:45,667 --> 00:15:50,667
God. No one's trying to
shoot me. I'm almost shaking.

365
00:15:50,667 --> 00:15:54,367
The chopper messed up something in
my head; I can't take more of that.

366
00:15:54,367 --> 00:15:55,933
I should get away from the river.

367
00:15:55,933 --> 00:15:59,400
This has all been a setup anyway, so
it kind of doesn't matter where I go.

368
00:15:59,400 --> 00:16:03,167
When you don't know anything,
all options are equally good.

369
00:16:03,167 --> 00:16:05,500
Maybe I could go to one of
those buildings in the distance

370
00:16:05,500 --> 00:16:08,767
and jump someone who looks
like me and swap clothes.

371
00:16:08,767 --> 00:16:11,654
Now would be--Oh shit. Radiation.

372
00:16:11,654 --> 00:16:14,467
Well... My Geiger counter isn't ticking.

373
00:16:14,467 --> 00:16:16,233
I'll just go in and take a peek.

374
00:16:16,233 --> 00:16:17,824
If it looks dicey, then...

375
00:16:18,467 --> 00:16:19,367
Fuck...

376
00:16:19,367 --> 00:16:20,333
Oh fuck!

377
00:16:20,667 --> 00:16:21,533
FEMALE VOICE: I've got something.

378
00:16:21,533 --> 00:16:23,500
They got me! This isn't happening!

379
00:16:23,500 --> 00:16:24,633
FEMALE VOICE: Okay, it's human.

380
00:16:24,633 --> 00:16:25,700
Think quick...

381
00:16:25,700 --> 00:16:26,567
FEMALE VOICE: Hello?

382
00:16:26,567 --> 00:16:27,100
What?

383
00:16:27,100 --> 00:16:29,700
FEMALE VOICE: Take it easy
in there. You're safe now.

384
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:31,433
Oh my God! They're gassing me!

385
00:16:31,433 --> 00:16:32,000
FEMALE VOICE: ...the scanning process.

386
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,533
[gagging]
FEMALE VOICE: We can't take any chances.

387
00:16:35,311 --> 00:16:36,137
...Kleiner...

